<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Late Classic period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 600–900</span> · Also known as Late Classic Maya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Late Classic is the period of Maya history from about 600 to 900 CE, when lowland Maya civilisation reached its height. Dozens of royal courts such as Tikal, Calakmul, Yaxchilan and Bonampak competed and built temples, palaces and carved monuments with hieroglyphic texts. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/classic-maya-collapse">Classic Maya collapse</a>, when most southern lowland cities were abandoned.</p></div>
